    "user_request_original": "Optimize an 8-layer anti-reflection coating on silicon substrate. Stack sequence from air side: Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), then semi-infinite si substrate. Incident medium is air at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Wavelength bands: 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. Each layer thickness is an independent optimization variable bounded between 20 nm and 400 nm. Objective: minimize weighted average reflectance across both wavelength bands while maximizing transmittance into silicon. Report best candidate thicknesses, reflectance spectra across both bands, and transmittance into substrate. Use gradient-based or evolutionary thickness optimization with multiple random initializations to avoid local minima.",
